      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Consent Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is the consent form?\", \"a\": \"A consent form is the document a person reads and signs before agreeing to a medical procedure or a research study. It explains what will happen and what could go wrong, and it says they may refuse. The signature records the decision and when it was made.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make my own consent form?\", \"a\": \"Start with the facts the signer needs, purpose and risks first, plus how to withdraw. Paste that text into Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> and describe who signs. It builds an online consent form that collects initials and a signature, then emails each signer a PDF copy.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an example of a consent form?\", \"a\": \"A dental extraction consent is a familiar consent form example: it names the tooth, lists risks such as dry socket and ends with a signature. Hospitals use a surgery consent form in the same way. In research, participants sign an informed consent form before they enroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a signed consent form?\", \"a\": \"A signed consent form is the completed copy: the text a person read, with a signature and a date at the bottom. It is what a clinic or study pulls out when someone later asks who agreed to what. Emergent keeps each one in a database you own, where staff can look it up by name or date.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the two forms of consent?\", \"a\": \"Express and implied. Express consent is stated outright, out loud or on paper, as when a patient signs before an extraction. Implied consent is read from behavior: a patient who rolls up a sleeve when the nurse lifts the flu shot. Any form of consent that may need proving later belongs in writing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an informed consent form?\", \"a\": \"An informed consent form records that a person understood the choice before signing, with the risks and the other options explained above the signature line. A simpler consent, such as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/photo-release-form'>photo release form</a>, may record only a yes. The person also gets time to ask questions before deciding.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does an IRB consent form need to include?\", \"a\": \"An IRB consent form needs every element the federal Common Rule requires, in text the board approved before the first participant signs. Store the approval date with each version, and let participants sign only the current one. Studies with minors add a parent consent form and the child's assent. A study that enrolls thousands hits no response cap on Emergent.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an online consent form be signed electronically?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Federal research rules allow a consent form to be signed in an electronic format. In practice that is a finger on a phone screen or a mouse on a laptop. A digital consent form should save the time of each signature along with the signer's name. Outside research, confirm the rules for your field and state before relying on it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an ethical consent form?\", \"a\": \"An ethical consent form makes saying no as simple as saying yes. It explains the study or procedure in plain words and asks without pressure. It also states that refusing costs the person nothing. In a consent form app, the decline button sits beside the accept button, and a withdrawal is one tap away.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you make a consent form in Spanish?\", \"a\": \"Whenever a US study enrolls people who read Spanish better than English: consent information has to be in language the participant understands. Have the IRB approve the Spanish text, then build both versions into one form. Each signer picks a language, and the record notes which one they signed.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
